-- #3377: `Int` is 63-bit and its arithmetic traps instead of wrapping —
-- `intMaxBound * 2` stops with E-INT-OVERFLOW on every engine.  SCALAR mode (no
-- ADT/closure/string, so useRef == False): the i64 never boxes, so this pins the
-- check at the arith op itself ($mdk_int_mul), not at the box seam.  The i64
-- product fits here; arith_int63_mul_i64_overflow_scalar covers one that does not.
-- expect-stderr: runtime error [E-INT-OVERFLOW]: 4611686018427387903 * 2 overflows Int
main = 4611686018427387903 * 2
